  "cover_text": "The court system in Sheridan, Arkansas is a government body like any other. Before a criminal can be charged and tried, they must first appear before the magistrate who presides over a proceeding as a judge. An initial meeting with a judge takes place at the courthouse. The judge's role is to keep records of everything that happens that day.\nThe local courthouse often has the same name as the city. All of the courthouses in Arkansas are named after the respective counties it serves. Thusjeon means \"country according to\" and Hillary, the result of reorganization, was named in the honor of Alexander Hamilton, one of the nation's first constitutional framers. The courthouse disharmony often results in a situation",
